 "text": "Toroidal transformers\nTorivac has more than thirty years of experience in the manufacture of all kinds of toroidal transformers. Toroidal transformers represent, like no other type, the ideal design of how a transformer should be. In fact, Faraday designed and wound the first transformer on a toroidal core. The toroidal cores manufactured by Torivac are built with grain oriented magnetic plate, with very low losses and high saturation induction and after being thermally treated, it allows reaching saturation values of up to 16,000 gauss. \n\nIn the toroidal transformer, the magnetic flux is uniformly concentrated on the core and, due to the absence of air gaps, vibrations are eliminated. Also, since the winding is distributed over the entire surface of the core, the noise caused by magnetostriction is practically eliminated and heat dissipation is favored. These details substantially improve the characteristics and performance of toroidal transformers compared to conventional transformers. \n\nThe stability and reliability of the power supply in Europe depends to a large extent on the quality of its industrial components, one of the most fundamental being conventional transformers. These devices are responsible for adapting electrical voltage levels for safe and efficient use in both domestic and industrial applications. In sectors such as automation, electronics and heavy machinery, choosing the right transformer is not a trivial matter. \n\nEspecially in markets such as Spain, where technical precision and European regulations define the standards, conventional transformers must pass rigorous tests to ensure long-lasting and safe performance. Despite the advance of new technologies, these models remain indispensable for their robustness, ease of maintenance and operational reliability. Its role as an intermediate and regulatory link in energy distribution continues to be irreplaceable.\n\nExplore subcategories\nTCi Series (printed circuit board enclosure)\nTT series transformers, encapsulated with epoxy resin, in polyamide 6 cases, internally connected to the pins for direct application on printed circuit boards. Raster between pins is 5mm and their number varies according to the size of the case. The connection can be configured according to the needs of each customer.\nLearn more\nTE Series\nThey are transformers of the TT series, encapsulated in epoxy resin, in polyamide 6 enclosures that extend the service life and improve the insulation of the transformer. They are ideal for humid environments Choosing reliable encapsulated toroidal transformers for demanding industrial environments, Torivac has established itself as one of the few European companies specialized in this field.\nLearn more\nTT Series\nThis TT series transformer is manufactured with a 230V primary and two identical secondaries, which allow to duplicate voltages or currents, connecting them in series or parallel, in a power range between 20VA and 220VA, supplied with individual boxes and mounting accessories.\nLearn more\n\nTorivac-Products\n\n×\n\nProducts\n\nTransformers\n\n+\n\nConventional transformer\n\nToroidal transformers\n\nVoltage variators - Adjustable autotransformers\n\n+\n\nCustom manufacturing\n\nDesktop equipment\n\nDouble Variator\n\nRegulating accessories\n\nSingle Phase Inverters\n\nThree-phase drives\n\nVoltage stabilizers\n\n+\n\nAVS Series Stabilizers: electromechanical with servo motor\n\nBAVS Series: Electronics\n\nRheostats and coiled potentiometers\n\n+\n\nCeramic rheostats\n\nPotentiometers\n\nEncapsulated coils\n\n+\n\nRound\n\nSquares\n\nChokes | Inductances | Toroidal Reactances\n\n+\n\nNuclei\n\n+\n\nPortaled\n\n+\n\nled 10mm\n\nled 3mm\n\nled 5mm\n\nled 8mm\n\nSockets\n\n+\n\nHB4 socket\n\nHSR4 safety socket\n\nSafety socket HBS4\n\nsafety socket HR4\n\nControl buttons\n\n+\n\nArrow Discs\n\nArrow hoops\n\nBM series control buttons (Matte)\n\nBM Series Covers\n\nBO series control buttons (bright)\n\nBO Series control buttons with line\n\nBO series covers\n\nCasing covers\n\nEstators\n\nGraded covers\n\nGraduated discs\n\nResistors : Load banks\n\n+\n\nBoxed\n\nBraking resistors\n\nCemented\n\nGrounding resistors\n\nHelical\n\nLoad banks\n\nStarting resistors\n\nElectronic equipment\n\n+\n\nConverters\n\nDC power supplies\n\nIndustrial control\n\nRenewable energies",
